  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "We prove Peter Luschny's conjecture in OEIS A323206, COMMENTS, revision 52 (first posed in revision 17, February 21, 2019): for all nonnegative n,k, the terminating hypergeometric value A(n,k) is odd precisely when n is even or k+2 is a positive power of two. Its coefficients are integer ballot numbers, and their sum is C_(k+1). Thus evaluation modulo two reduces to the constant coefficient or a Catalan number. A binary product describes the complete coefficient support; its consequences include the linked rows, columns, three adjacent diagonals, antidiagonal sums and generalized ballot triangle.",
